      "description": "Simple matchstick polygons (closed self-avoiding unit-edge polygons) on the cyclotomic ring Z[zeta_9], with perimeter <= 18, canonicalized by free (full dihedral) symmetry. Contains 503397962 sequences. It is the order-9 sub-ring of Z[zeta_18] (Z[zeta_9] has no native lattice here, so it is enumerated as the directions that are multiples of 2, via --step 2); each stored turn is a Z[zeta_18] unit (always even) equal to 2 times the Z[zeta_9] turn -- divide stored values by 2 to read Z[zeta_9] turns. See README.md (Turn-angle units). Self-describing tilezz-rat-dafsa-blocks asset (schemas alongside).",
